# Copy this file to  .env  and fill in what you use. .env is gitignored: never commit a real key.
# Without a key the product still works: the bill's text and the Aadhaar QR are read by plain rules,
# and the dashboard says "Model off" so you always know which path ran.

# ---- Reading the documents with AI (off by default) ----
# With AI on, Gemini reads the electricity bill and the Aadhaar as soon as each is uploaded and fills the
# details: the bill first (the portal matches the DISCOM's records), the Aadhaar for what the bill lacks.
# The rules and the Aadhaar QR still run first. The full Aadhaar number is stored only encrypted.
# Turn it on with BOTH of these:
SOLARA_USE_AI=1
GEMINI_API_KEY=key1,key2
#   One key, or several comma-separated with no quotes. Keys from different Google Cloud projects have
#   separate quotas: on a rate limit (429) the next key is tried.
#   A key set in the Windows environment wins over this file: remove it there if it is an old one.
# Or, instead of Gemini, ONE of:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# Optional: the model. Defaults are gemini-3.6-flash / claude-sonnet-5-5 / gpt-4.1-mini.
# SOLARA_MODEL=gemini-3.6-flash
# Optional: Gemini models tried in order when the one above is busy (5xx) or too slow (25 s).
# SOLARA_MODEL_BACKUP=gemini-3-flash-preview,gemini-flash-lite-latest

# ---- The client's templates (kept out of the repository: it is public) ----
# The agreement draft (a PDF) and the bank quotations (Word, one per amount, named like
# "Bank Quotation - 125000.docx"). The installation-cost choices are read from the quotation folder.
# By default both are looked for beside the code, in "agreement draft" and "Quoatation (all range)".
# SOLARA_AGREEMENT_DIR=D:\solara\agreement draft
# SOLARA_QUOTES_DIR=D:\solara\quotations

# ---- The installer named on generated close-out documents ----
# SOLARA_VENDOR_NAME=Your Solar Company Pvt Ltd
# SOLARA_VENDOR_SIGNATORY=Name of the authorised signatory
# SOLARA_VENDOR_PHONE=+91 98XXXXXXXX          (shown to customers on their document page)

# ---- Solara's internet address ----
# Customers open their document and signing links on their own phones,
# so links must use an address reachable from the internet, never localhost:
# SOLARA_PUBLIC_URL=https://solara.example.in
